Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:</strong></span></td><td>The release of sperms into&nbsp;the seminiferous tubules is called spermiation.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td>Spermiogenesis is the process of formation of sperms from spermatogonia.</td></tr></tbody></table>
In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the option given below :<br>1. <strong>Statement I </strong>is incorrect but <strong>Statement II </strong>is correct.<br>2. Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II </strong>are correct.<br>3. Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II </strong>are incorrect.<br>4. <strong>Statement I </strong>is correct but <strong>Statement II </strong>is incorrect.

Match the following columns and select the correct option&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 500px;"><tbody><tr><td></td><td>Column-I</td><td></td><td>Column-II</td></tr><tr><td>a.</td><td>Corpus luteum</td><td>(i)</td><td>Secretes inhibin in males to inhibit FSH</td></tr><tr><td>b.</td><td>Sertoli cells</td><td>(ii)</td><td>Secretes a hormone to maintain pregnancy</td></tr><tr><td>c.</td><td>Seminal vesicle</td><td>(iii)</td><td>Transforms ruptured Graafian follicle into corpus lutem&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>d.</td><td>Luteinizing hormone</td><td>(iv)</td><td>Its secretion constitutes major part of semen&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>
1. a(ii), b(i), c(iv), d(iii)<br>2.&nbsp;a(i), b(ii), c(iii), d(iv)<br>3.&nbsp;a(iv), b(iii), c(ii), d(i)<br>4.&nbsp;a(iii), b(iv), c(i), d(ii)<br>&nbsp;

Read the following statements (a-d):&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 500px;"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>Inner cell mass gets differentiated as the embryo after implantation&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>After attachment of embryo with uterus, the uterine cells divide rapidly and cover the blastocyst&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>The blastocyst continues to divide and transforms into morula&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>After implantation, the blastocyst becomes embedded within myometrium of uterus&nbsp;</td></tr></tbody></table>
Choose the option containing all correct statements<br>1. (a) and (b)<br>2. (b) and (c)<br>3. (c) and (d)<br>4. (a) and (d)&nbsp;
